meta {
  name: list components
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}library/components/?ordering=name
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ordering: name
  ~search: motor
  ~category: 1
  ~unit: 1
  ~stock_status: below_minimum
  ~min_price: 10
  ~max_price: 500
  ~project: 1
  ~archived: false
  ~p: 1
  ~page_size: 25
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  The component list (FR-1.3), paginated at 25 rows. Any role. Each row has
  the image URL, name, part number, category, unit, `total_quantity` across
  all chambers, `stock_status`, prices, `locations` (chamber codes) and
  `updated_at`.

  `stock_status` is `OUT_OF_STOCK` (total 0), `LOW_STOCK` (total at or below
  minimum) or `IN_STOCK`. `is_low_stock` is true whenever the total is at or
  below the minimum (FR-6.10).

  Filters (FR-1.5): `category`, `unit`, `stock_status` (`in_stock` |
  `out_of_stock` | `below_minimum`), `min_price` / `max_price` (last buying
  price), `project` (components taken against that project), `archived`
  (`false` default | `true` | `all`).
  Search (FR-1.6): `search` matches name, part number, description and
  location code.
  Sorting (FR-1.4): `ordering` = `name` | `part_number` | `category` |
  `total_quantity` | `last_buying_price` | `updated_at`, prefix `-` for
  descending.


  ## API example response
  {
